\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Top Markets Headlines at 3 AM ET: Oil prices, stock futures inch higher as U.S. and Iran reportedly agree to halt attacks | BIS ...\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Oil prices, stock futures inch higher as U.S. and Iran reportedly agree to halt attacks\par \par \uc2 Oil prices rose Sunday and U.S. stock-index futures advanced, after the U.S. and Iran reportedly agreed to halt attacks after repeatedly exchanging fire in the Persian Gulf over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 BIS Sees Peril for Economy, Financial System in AI Investment Boom\par \par \uc2 Fierce competition will dominate \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks driving investment spending to excessive levels that could tip some economies into recession, the \uc2 Bank for International Settlements\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 China Adds More Japanese Entities to Export Control List\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chinese commerce ministry\uc2  said it added 20 Japanese entities to an export control list that prohibits Chinese firms from selling dual-use products to those companies\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Warsh's Words Could Prove the Best Tool for Fighting Inflation. They're Already Working\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Kevin Warsh\uc2  has vowed to curb the central bank's communications. But they may be the most benign tool with which to shape monetary policy, for now.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 The Trillion-Dollar Borrowing Binge Lifting the Stock Market to Risky Heights\par \par \uc2 Leveraged funds and margin debt have grown to unprecedented levels this year.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Korea's Chips Rally Is Driving Its Stock Market Into a Danger Zone\par \par \uc2 The rally driven by the global \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  boom has exposed structural vulnerabilities in a stock market unaccustomed to wild swings.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 How Some Private-Equity Managers Collect Big Fees on Paper Gains\par \par \uc2 The fee structures are among the pitfalls of investing in semiliquid funds.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Forget the 'Sell America' trade: Why U.S. markets keep proving the naysayers wrong\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors are still pouring money into U.S. assets, and the dollar remains the undisputed global reserve currency.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 A $55 Billion Safety Net? Government Tab to Prop Up American Farms Is Rising\par \par \uc2 President Trump's latest request extends a run of interventions intended to help the nation's agricultural economy.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Your Dream Home Is Out There. A Glut Is on the Way.\par \par \uc2 The housing shortage will end in the coming decade as demand eases because of smaller generations and thinning immigration, new figures show. And, best of all, prices will drop.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Week Ahead for FX, Bonds: U.S. Jobs Data in Focus as Markets Search for Clues on Fed Rate Path\par \par \uc2 U.S. jobs data could confirm indications that the economy is robust as investors gauge whether and when the Fed might raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Chip Makers Are Profiting Off AI at the Expense of Just About Everyone Else\par \par \uc2 We are witnessing an extraordinary transfer of cash from the providers of AI-and, perhaps one day, AI users-to memory-chip makers.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 AI turbocharged the stock market. Now it's firing up the economy.\par \par \uc2 A modern-day gold rush is giving a big boost to U.S. GDP.\par \par \uc2 ----\par \par \uc2 Kevin Warsh\uc2  Invokes \uc2 Alan Greenspan\uc2  to Shrink the Fed-and Strengthen Its Chair\par \par \uc2 The approach of the new \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  head might not always 