\par\par \b \uc2 Tech, Media & Telecom Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 10:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering Technology, Media and Telecom. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires at 4:20 ET, 12:20 ET and 16:50 ET.\par \par \uc2 0513 GMT - Uncertainty over \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2 ' and \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2 's potential capital-expenditure is likely pressuring their share prices, says \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 's Jing Jie Yu in commentary. The two companies could be planning to spend around a combined 2 quadrillion won over the next decade, nearly double \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 's capex estimates. This could include \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2 's plans to invest in \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  data centers, with its Yongin fab cluster commitments already expected at 600 trillion won, he notes. Should \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2 's AI data center commitment and its potential capex plans be separate, the analyst flags material risk of oversupply for memory producers, given that demand tends to taper off during the tail years of capex cycles. \uc2 Samsung\uc2  shares fall 6.5% to 317,000 won, while \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  shares drop 4.7% to 2,548,000 won. (megan.cheah@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0446 GMT - \uc2 LG Display\uc2  could post a wider 2Q loss than the market expects due to a one-off cost for business restructuring, \uc2 Nomura\uc2 's Eon Hwang and YJ Kim say. The South Korean flat-screen maker's operating loss is expected to come in at around 96 billion won for the April-June period, compared with the market consensus estimate of a 55 billion won loss, the analysts reckon. Excluding the one-off cost, the firm's major business likely improved, they say. Its organic light-emitting diode TV panel sales likely rose 9.7% from a year earlier in 2Q, driven by the World Cup soccer games, with its OLED monitor shipments likely having jumped 86%, they add. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0445 GMT - The recent selloff of Chinese internet stocks has created a compelling opportunity in terms of valuations, \uc2 Citi\uc2  analysts say in a research note. China's internet sector has underperformed as it has been treated as a source of funds to buy AI hardware stocks, the analysts say. As a result, the Hang Seng Index is down 11% so far this year while the Kospi is up 100% despite recent volatility. The analysts think \uc2 PDD\uc2  and \uc2 Meituan\uc2  are now trading near their five-year trough multiples. "With solid net cash positions and outstanding buyback programs, we expect companies to accelerate their buyback pace, and we believe that fundamentals will eventually prevail," they say. (sherry.qin@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0336 GMT - Apple's reported interest in buying \uc2 CXMT\uc2  memory chips is a strong validation of its technological progress, \uc2 Citi\uc2  analysts say in a research note. According to a media report, Apple is lobbying the Trump administration for approval to buy DRAM from \uc2 CXMT\uc2  amid surging memory costs. \uc2 CXMT\uc2  is currently included in the Pentagon's list of restricted Chinese companies. \uc2 Citi\uc2  reckons that securing approval to procure \uc2 CXMT\uc2  memory could prove challenging in the current U.S. political climate. "Regardless of whether Apple gets the purchase approval, its consideration of \uc2 CXMT\uc2  as a potential supplier shifts market perception of \uc2 CXMT\uc2  from a domestic substitution play to a credible global No.4 DRAM maker," they say.(sherry.qin@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0330 GMT - \uc2 Sarana Menara Nusantara\uc2  is likely undertaking disciplined expansion, \uc2 UOB Kay Hian\uc2  analysts say in a research report as the brokerage maintains the stock's buy rating. The Indonesian telecom tower operator continues to expand its asset base in a disciplined manner, ending 1Q with around 36,572 towers and 181,700 kilometers of fibre optic network, the analysts note. Management guides for another 400-600 new towers in 2026, with stable capital expenditure of around 5 trillion rupiah. However, the brokerage lowers its stock target price to 530.00 rupiah from 620.00 rupiah as it uses a narrower reference period of valuation to better reflect structural de-rating of the sector. Shares are 1.1% higher at 378.00 rupiah. (ronnie.harui@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0126 GMT - Malaysia's technology sector appears to remain well below previous valuation peaks despite improving earnings prospects and growing exposure to global AI and data center spending, Maybank IB analysts Lucas Sim and Justin Yeoh say in a note. AI or data center-related demand could remain the sector's main growth driver through 2026, supported by sustained spending by major cloud companies, they reckon. Continued digitalization and a largely domestic business base provide resilience against geopolitical risks to the software sector, they add. \uc2 Maybank\uc2  upgrades Malaysia's technology sector's rating to positive from neutral despite the near-term currency headwind, and peg \uc2 Vitrox\uc2 , Pentamaster, Northeast and \uc2 Itmax System\uc2  as top buys. (yingxian.wong@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2026 04:20 ET (08:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t000v8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
