\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: Fypro.ai Officially Launches at VidCon Anaheim 2026, Introducing an AI Growth Engine for Creator-Led Commerce\b0\par\par\uc2 954 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 16:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 ANAHEIM, CA, June 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Fypro.ai officially launched at VidCon Anaheim 2026, which was held June 25-27 at the Anaheim Convention Center. The launch introduced the AI-powered storefront platform to creators, brands, and the broader creator-economy community with a series of live product demonstrations at Booth 5013 and a presentation by Caelith \uc2 AI Co\uc2 -Founder and COO Steven Zhou. The event also saw the debut of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeWdA6_xOm1oXC1g-t9J5mH82Eys2rZITrkM_8p0ZO4GB8Ac_8pWvV-zoCqnXZ_GTVA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeWdA6_xOm1oXC1g-t9J5mH82Eys2rZITrkM_8p0ZO4GB8Ac_8pWvV-zoCqnXZ_GTVA}}}\uc2 == fypro.ai Creator Contest, marking the company's entry into the rapidly-evolving creator commerce landscape.\par \par \uc2 The launch can be viewed as reflecting a growing shift within the creator economy, wherein creators increasingly seek to build sustainable businesses beyond advertising revenue and affiliate links.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the three-day event, fypro.ai demonstrated how \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  can help creators by simplifying storefront creation, commerce operations, and long-term customer management. In a nutshell, the platform helps transform audience engagement into owned income.\par \par \uc2 A Unified AI Platform for Creator Commerce\par \par \uc2 Fypro.ai is designed to be an AI growth engine, helping creators build and grow their own web commerce businesses from a single platform. Rather than relying on disconnected creator tools, multiple software subscriptions and third-party marketplaces--as has often been necessary in the past--fypro.ai combines commerce infrastructure with AI-powered recommendations tailored specifically for creators.\par \par \uc2 The platform is meant to enable creators to launch personalized online storefronts in several minutes. And it does so while providing ongoing AI assistance surrounding product discovery, content planning and analytics, customer relationship management, and operational workflows. Fypro.ai's approach to reducing administrative complexity for creatives is built around three core pillars: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Personalized growth recommendations specific to each creator account's \par       audience and content performance \par  \par    -- End-to-end commerce infrastructure supporting AI-assisted product \par       selection, storefront management, checkout, orders, and fulfillment \par  \par    -- Creator ownership of customer relationships, brand assets, and \par       first-party data \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By combining these capabilities, fypro.ai positions creators to build businesses they own rather than relying entirely on external platforms for monetization, freeing them to spend more time producing content and engaging their communities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Steven Zhou Outlines the Future of Creator-Owned Businesses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During his presentation on June 27 in Room 210 AB, Steven Zhou discussed the new stage of development that creator commerce is currently entering. While creators have become increasingly skilled at building audiences and generating engagement, he raised the point that many still face operational barriers to building sustainable businesses around their content.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The presentation emphasized that AI can and should do more than automate isolated tasks. It should function as the operating system behind a creator's business, helping them identify opportunities, streamlining decision-making, and managing the infrastructure needed to grow long-term revenue.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Creators have done the work of building an audience that trusts them. The business side shouldn't require another career or a full team," said Steven Zhou. "We built fypro.ai because creators need the infrastructure built around their specific account, interests, lifestyle and audience, not a generic template."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Zhou illustrated throughout the session how AI-powered storefronts can help creators move beyond one-time campaigns and toward repeatable, creator-owned commerce models. Case studies presented during the session highlighted individual creators across multiple verticals--lifestyle, beauty, pet content--who used AI-assisted content planning and storefront operations to improve audience engagement while creating new opportunities for monetization.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data shared during Steven Zhou's presentation underscored the platform's early momentum. According to data provided by the company, fypro.ai has: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Analyzed more than 4 million viral \f28 \uc2 \f2 TikTok\f28 \uc2 \f2  videos \par  \par    -- Grown to support a community of more than 2,000 active creators \par  \par    -- Collectively driven over 10 million views \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fypro.ai's Presence at VidCon\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition to Steven Zhou's presentation, fypro.ai's presence at VidCon included live demonstrations of the platform at Booth 5013. Visitors got an opportunity to experience the platform in person, including AI-powered content insights, storefront creation workflows, integrated commerce tools and personalized creator diagnostics showcased by the fypro.ai team. Attendees also met with the team to discuss how AI can help support every stage of the creator commerce journey.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As part of the official launch, fypro.ai introduced the \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeSiM4EEmRTKl6gN_9-kyMgnjeYaj9WuEyICAk2FKQZUZE4VnGZWgrz3fAZjLcxXPZA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeSiM4EEmRTKl6gN_9-kyMgnjeYaj9WuEyICAk2FKQZUZE4VnGZWgrz3fAZjLcxXPZA}}}\uc2 \f2 == fypro.ai Creator Contest, extending the company's creator-first strategy beyond the event itself. Running from June 25 through July 31, 2026, the contest is an extension of fypro.ai's creator-first launch strategy, encouraging creators to test the platform, build their storefronts, and drive content-led commerce performance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Participants can enter the fypro.ai \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVedI0JiNd40P_a26GZ-d-h1-nlVpfwWsufwhPhP2kosBWoCXXB7SHQhxTcDQzaxf1YA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVedI0JiNd40P_a26GZ-d-h1-nlVpfwWsufwhPhP2kosBWoCXXB7SHQhxTcDQzaxf1YA}}}\uc2 \f2 == Creator Contest by scanning the QR code displayed at the fypro's booth or by visiting the official contest landing page. Winners of the Best Store Award and Best Content Traffic Award will be announced via the Fypro Discord community on July 31, 2026.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Building on the Momentum from VidCon\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fypro.ai is now live at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeaifvQSK0dmTbNY8feJIM41txoF1VncpJrtAa44qn3C6i47w3lJAo_ejl0g-TFvbiA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeaifvQSK0dmTbNY8feJIM41txoF1VncpJrtAa44qn3C6i47w3lJAo_ejl0g-TFvbiA}}}\uc2 \f2 == fypro.ai, where creators can explore the platform, launch their own AI-powered storefronts, and join the fypro.ai \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeWAm0-O_jYY2p618nkvHfyARu35ctt58orKHml66yXH6bcSCh66b2TI-jSGJ3DHP6A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=k5LpWsKwgW_g6Xy6ctkVeWAm0-O_jYY2p618nkvHfyARu35ctt58orKHml66yXH6bcSCh66b2TI-jSGJ3DHP6A}}}\uc2 \f2 == Creator Contest before July 31, 2026. Looking beyond VidCon Anaheim 2026, the company continues to work toward equipping creators with the AI infrastructure to grow sustainable, creator-owned businesses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Caelith.ai pr@caelith.ai\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 29, 2026 10:05 ET (14:05 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t002ah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
