\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 SoftBank Group\uc2  Shares Fall 11.5% to Y6,300\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2026\par 03:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 25 Jun 2026 23:57 ET  \uc2 SoftBank Group\uc2  Shares Slide as AI Rollercoaster Trade Continues\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Yang Jie\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 SoftBank Group Corp.\uc2  fell over 13% Friday as worries about valuations and profitability in \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  spurred a broad selloff across Asia technology stocks.\par \par \uc2 The drop in \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 , seen as a proxy for the AI trade, puts the stock on track for one of its biggest one-day percentage losses in nearly two years. Japan's benchmark Nikkei index was down over 4%, with other tech names like \uc2 Advantest\uc2  and \uc2 Kioxia\uc2  dropping over 9% each.\par \par \uc2 Like other AI plays, \uc2 SoftBank\uc2  shares have been caught in a pattern of sharp swings recently as market sentiment toward AI-related equities flits between euphoria over the technology's long-term promise and pessimism regarding near-term monetization and sky-high valuations.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the latest downturn in the tech investment conglomerate's stock was likely triggered by a report that ChatGPT maker \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  is considering delaying its initial public offering.\par \par \uc2 In a report on Thursday citing sources familiar with the matter, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  said \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  is leaning toward holding off its initial public offering until next year due to concerns around market volatility.\par \par \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  didn't immediately respond to a request for comment sent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A delay of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's blockbuster IPO would be seen as a headwind for \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 , which is building up an approximately 13% stake in the AI pioneer worth $64.6 billion. When news of the ChatGPT maker's plans to go public started making the rounds in May, \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 's shares surged nearly 20%.\par \par \uc2 An overnight drop in shares of \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 's chip design subsidiary, \uc2 Arm Holdings\uc2 , likely also contributed to the negative mood.\par \par \uc2 Friday's decline caps a roller-coaster week for \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 's stock, which ended the previous session 8% higher but slumped 10% on Monday. Tech names elsewhere in Asia have experienced similar volatility, exemplified by the huge gains and losses in South Korea's tech-heavy Kospi index - another AI proxy.\par \par \uc2 Despite the recent chill that has swept the tech sector, some say it's too early to call the end of the AI rally just yet.\par \par \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 's stock remains 42% higher year to date and its founder and chief executive, \uc2 Masayoshi Son\uc2 , expected the AI momentum to continue saying earlier this week that the world is only at the very beginning of the AI revolution that will re-define every industry.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the week, blowout guidance from Micron sparked a furious rebound in AI-related shares. Tickmill Group's Patrick Munnelly said the market reaction suggests investors are still willing to treat AI as a boom rather than a bubble.\par \par \uc2 News Corp\uc2 , owner of The Wall Street Journal and Dow Jones Newswires, has a content-licensing partnership with \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Yang Jie\uc2  at jie.yang@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 23:57 ET (03:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260626em6q0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
