\par\par \b \uc2 ON Semiconductor Joins 'Edge AI' Market With $7 Billion Acquisition. The Stock Falls. -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nate Wolf \par \uc2 337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 23:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 ON Semiconductor\uc2  has agreed to buy internet-of-things company \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  as it vies to bring \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  from data centers into the physical world.\par \par \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  shareholders will receive 1.35 shares of \uc2 Onsemi\uc2  stock for each \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  share in the all-stock deal, representing an enterprise value of around $7 billion.\par \par \uc2 Onsemi\uc2  stock dropped 8.3% to $108.85 in after-hours trading Thursday. Shares have surged 119% this year despite sluggish revenue growth because valuations across the semiconductor industry have soared.\par \par \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  investors, meanwhile, secured a nice premium for their shares. The stock was up 11% to $140 on Thursday evening.\par \par \uc2 Known for making analog chips for automotive and industrial markets, \uc2 Onsemi\uc2  has grown its sales to data centers and but hasn't been a central player in the AI boom. The company sees an opening in edge AI, however, which refers to computing done on local devices rather than in the cloud.\par \par \uc2 In particular, \uc2 Synaptics\uc2 ' combination of processors, connectivity solutions, and software platform can help power physical AI applications, such as autonomous driving and robotics.\par \par \uc2 "As \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves beyond the cloud and into the physical world, including automotive and industrial, the next phase of innovation will depend on systems that can sense, decide, act and adapt in real time," said \uc2 Onsemi\uc2  CEO \uc2 Hassane El-Khoury\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Moving into physical AI could expand \uc2 Onsemi\uc2 's total addressable market by between $30 billion and $243 billion by 2030, the company estimated. The acquisition is expected to boost adjusted earnings per share within 18 months of closing in mid-2027, with an expected $200 million in annual synergies.\par \par \uc2 Write to Nate Wolf at nate.wolf@barrons.com\par \par \uc2 This content was created by Barron's, which is operated by Dow Jones & Co. Barron's is published independently from Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 17:54 ET (21:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p003wq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
