\par\par \b \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  Just Revealed Its Mystery Big Tech Customer -- and Its Stock Is Rising -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 By George Glover and Adam Clark \par \uc2 512 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 21:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  stock advanced Thursday after the chip maker raised its non-handset sales target and revealed that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  parent \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  would be using a new data-center chip.\par \par \uc2 Shares gained 5.9% to $209.10 on Thursday, paring a premarket surge of more than 10%. The S&P 500 slipped 0.1% after stellar earnings from memory-chip maker \uc2 Micron Technology\uc2  failed to fully revive the AI trade.\par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  late Wednesday raised its fiscal 2029 non-handset revenue target to $40 billion, almost double its previous guidance. The company also expects $15 billion of data-center sales by that point.\par \par \uc2 Just hours earlier, \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  revealed at an investor day that \uc2 Meta\uc2  would use its Dragonfly C1000 central processing units when they become available in 2028.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's Azure cloud division will use another of \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2 's new products, its High Bandwidth Compute (HBC) chip architecture, expected in mid-2027.\par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  CFO \uc2 Akash Palkhiwala\uc2  told Barron's that the HBC packaging of logic and memory components can deliver high perfomance and bandwidth at low power.\par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2 's push into data centers comes as it seeks to diversify away from the smartphones, tablets, and gaming devices powered by its chips. \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  expects handsets to make up just one-third of its revenue by fiscal 2029, down from 72% in fiscal 2025.\par \par \uc2 "While we're coming in late, we're coming in with technology advantages and something unique that solves the problems that these companies have, " Palkhiwala said.\par \par \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  also said Wednesday that it had agreed to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  infrastructure software company Modular in a $3.9 billion stock deal as it looks to bulk out its AI portfolio.\par \par \uc2 Modular has developed an AI programming language that is positioned as a competitor to \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's dominant CUDA and could help put \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  at the center of the sector.\par \par \uc2 "The entire strategy here is to have an industry standard stack that is completely open source that can be deployed by any customers, on \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  chips, but also on competitive chips," Palkhiwala said.\par \par \uc2 The flurry of announcements, coupled with Micron's strong results, arrive as chip stocks have struggled in recent days. Investors have fretted about how long so-called hyperscalers such as \uc2 Meta\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  can maintain their aggressive data-center spending.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts still aren't convinced the diversification strategy will pay off. "While data-center targets exceeded our expectations, we think it's early days," said KeyBanc's John Vinh, who rates shares Sector Weight.\par \par \uc2 Susquehanna\uc2  analyst \uc2 Christopher Rolland\uc2  raised his price target for the stock to $190 from $160 but maintained his Neutral rating, citing "headwinds in the mobile market."\par \par \uc2 Write to George Glover at george.glover@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 This content was created by Barron's, which is operated by Dow Jones & Co. Barron's is published independently from Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 15:04 ET (19:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p0037v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
