\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 Adtran Holdings, Inc.\uc2  Appoints \uc2 Anne DelSanto\uc2  to Board of Directors\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 22:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HUNTSVILLE, Ala.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--June 25, 2026-- \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Adtran Holdings, Inc.\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NASDAQ: ADTN and FSE: QH9), a leading global provider of networking and communications solutions, today announced the appointment of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anne DelSanto\f28 \uc2 \f2  as an independent member of its Board of Directors effective July 1, 2026. The appointment aligns with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adtran\f28 \uc2 \f2 's expanding relevance beyond its service provider core, into cloud infrastructure, AI-driven networking, and enterprise software, markets where Ms. DelSanto has spent the majority of her career.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Ms. DelSanto brings more than 30 years of experience in the global technology industry focused on cloud computing, software-as-a-service (SaaS), \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and enterprise go-to-market strategy. Her professional career included executive operational and technical roles at companies including \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 , \uc2 Oracle\uc2 , and \uc2 IBM\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. DelSanto currently serves on the board of directors of \uc2 Advanced Energy\uc2  (NASDAQ: AEIS), a company that designs and manufactures precision power solutions for hyperscale AI, semiconductor, and industrial markets, and on the boards of private technology companies, \uc2 Axonius\uc2  and \uc2 StackAdapt\uc2 . She formerly served on the boards of \uc2 Juniper Networks\uc2  and \uc2 New Relic\uc2 , both during their tenure of being publicly traded.\par \par \uc2 "Anne's experience building and scaling cloud and SaaS platforms will be a valuable addition to our Board," said \uc2 Tom Stanton\uc2 , Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of \uc2 Adtran Holdings, Inc.\uc2  "Her relevant public board experience combined with her experience with hyperscalers, AI-driven infrastructure, and next-generation service provider solutions aligns with \uc2 Adtran\uc2 's strategic direction. We are delighted to welcome her."\par \par \uc2 Ms. DelSanto holds a Bachelor of Science in mathematics with a concentration in computer science from \uc2 St. John's University\uc2  and a Master of Science in administrative studies from Boston College. She has also completed advanced governance studies at Stanford University Law School's Directors' College.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 Adtran\par \par \uc2 ADTRAN Holdings, Inc.\uc2  (NASDAQ: ADTN and FSE: QH9) is the parent company of \uc2 Adtran, Inc.\uc2 , a leading global provider of open, disaggregated networking and communications solutions that enable voice, data, video and internet communications across any network infrastructure. From the cloud edge to the subscriber edge, \uc2 Adtran\uc2  empowers communications service providers around the world to manage and scale services that connect people, places and things. \uc2 Adtran\uc2  solutions are used by service providers, private enterprises, government organizations and millions of individual users worldwide. \uc2 ADTRAN Holdings, Inc.\uc2  is also the majority shareholder of \uc2 Adtran Networks SE\uc2 , formerly \uc2 ADVA Optical Networking SE\uc2 . Find more at Adtran.com, \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  and X.\par \par \uc2 Published by\par \par \uc2 ADTRAN Holdings, Inc.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.adtran.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.adtran.com}}}\par \par \uc2 View source version on businesswire.com: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260625660140/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260625660140/en/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     CONTACT:    For media \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gareth Spence\f28 \par \p