\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 onsemi\uc2  to Acquire \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  to Enable the Next Generation of Intelligent Systems for Physical AI\b0\par\par\uc2 2,953 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 22:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Accelerates \f28 \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's evolution, building on its strength in power and \par       sensing to become a leading provider of intelligent systems -- expanding \par       from AI data centers into Physical AI \par  \par    -- Increases \f28 \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's total addressable market by $30 billion to $243 \par       billion by 2030 \par  \par    -- Positions \f28 \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \uc2 \f2  at the intersection of Power, Sense, Connected Compute \par       and Control -- the four pillars of Physical AI -- which enable machines \par       to sense, decide, act and adapt in the physical world \par  \par    -- Would combine complementary portfolios to drive significant customer \par       value and deepen customer engagements \f28 \par \par \uc2 SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. & SAN JOSE, Calif., June 25, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- \uc2 onsemi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=gqse2tEhDp8n6YJ5WHnDnlWLwS2gk8vmLspcPmK2dJahfHUEhFqTXXCuLgXJ1fH8FhK8xSb4RfssKuqOQiz5lA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=gqse2tEhDp8n6YJ5WHnDnlWLwS2gk8vmLspcPmK2dJahfHUEhFqTXXCuLgXJ1fH8FhK8xSb4RfssKuqOQiz5lA}}}\uc2 == (Nasdaq: ON) and \uc2 Synaptics Incorporated{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=lK4yFPha-F6Z2TsmUkm_1gwIGuGTTvMtDxSDuseCr6TPMRgc2thA4hwa1ntp9KScroo5Fav5CPxWqyTMNagv8TC7thEaWkVPKB4pmJT493c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=lK4yFPha-F6Z2TsmUkm_1gwIGuGTTvMtDxSDuseCr6TPMRgc2thA4hwa1ntp9KScroo5Fav5CPxWqyTMNagv8TC7thEaWkVPKB4pmJT493c}}}\uc2 = (Nasdaq: SYNA) today announced they have entered into a definitive agreement under which \uc2 onsemi\uc2  has agreed to acquire \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  in an all-stock transaction, representing a total enterprise value of approximately $7 billion. The transaction value reflects a fixed exchange ratio of 1.350 shares of \uc2 onsemi\uc2  common stock for each \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  share and represents an approximately 19% premium to the volume weighted average closing prices of \uc2 onsemi\uc2  and \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  over the last 10 trading days.\par \par \uc2 The combination would accelerate \uc2 onsemi\uc2 's evolution toward global leadership in intelligent systems. By adding \uc2 Synaptics\uc2 ' differentiated Edge AI compute franchise and strong portfolio of human-machine interface and wireless connectivity solutions, \uc2 onsemi\uc2  is expected to extend its capabilities beyond power and sensing to intelligent systems, delivering greater value to a broad range of end markets. Building on \uc2 onsemi\uc2 's expertise in automotive, industrial and AI data center, the combined platform is intended to position \uc2 onsemi\uc2  at the center of Physical AI, with the potential to expand \uc2 onsemi\uc2 's TAM by $30 billion to $243 billion by 2030.\par \par \uc2 "As \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves beyond the cloud and into the physical world, including automotive and industrial, the next phase of innovation will depend on systems that can sense, decide, act and adapt in real time," said \uc2 Hassane El-Khoury\uc2 , President and CEO of \uc2 onsemi\uc2 . "This shift towards Physical AI will require Power, Sense, Connected Compute and Control to work together seamlessly. The addition of \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  helps position \uc2 onsemi\uc2  at the intersection of these four pillars, enabling us to capture a significantly larger AI opportunity that extends beyond AI data center and into edge applications. This transaction would add immediate connected compute capabilities, expand our software and ecosystem reach and position \uc2 onsemi\uc2  to deliver greater value as customers increasingly seek intelligent systems."\par \par \uc2 "Today's announcement marks an important step in accelerating \uc2 Synaptics\uc2 ' growth and leadership in Edge AI and Physical AI," said Rahul Patel, \uc2 Synaptics\uc2  President and CEO. "Together with \uc2 onsemi\uc2 , we will combine \uc2 Synaptics\uc2 ' strengths in AI-native compute, connectivity, and human-machine interface with \uc2 onsemi\uc2 's leadership in intelligent power and sensing to offer customers integrated solutions and development platforms across every layer of the Edge AI stack, deepening customer engagement and expanding across a greater total addressable market. The all-stock structure allows our shareholders to participate in the compelling growth and value creation opportunities ahead, and I look forward to working with the \uc2 onsemi\uc2  leadership team to help realize the full value of this combination."\par \par \uc2 Compelling Strategic and Financial Rationale\par \par \uc2 The combination is expected to deliver substantial value: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Enables capabilities from AI Infrastructure to Physical AI: \f28 \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \uc2 \f2  is \par       already well-positioned across the AI infrastructure ecosystem, from the \par       energy grid to the data center core. This transaction is expected to \par       extend that reach to the intelligent edge, enabling \f28 \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \uc2 \f2  to address \par       additional end markets while enhancing its capabilities to become a \par       provider of integrated, system-level solutions across Power, Sense, \par       Connected Compute and Control. This compelling combination would enable \par       systems that can sense, decide, act and adapt in real time across \par       Physical AI applications, including autonomous driving, robotics, and \par       AR/VR. \par  \par    -- Adds a proven, scalable Edge AI connected compute platform to \f28 \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Synaptics\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' Astra platform combines purpose-built AI processors and NPUs \par       for multimodal intelligence with an industry-leading wireless \par       connectivity portfolio spanning Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and GPS and a full \par       open-source software stack for rapid deployment. \par  \par    -- Complementary portfolios designed to unlock significant revenue growth \par       with scale: The combination of two highly complementary portfolios would \par       allow onsemi to accelerate its innovation and product roadmap to capture \par       higher dollar content per platform while fostering deeper long-term \par       customer engagement. This is anticipated to increase onsemi's exposure to \par       higher-value, differentiated system solutions with embedded IP and \par       software, supporting improved mix, margin expansion and durable growth. \par  \par    -- Attractive financial profile: The transaction is expected to be accretive \par       to non-GAAP EPS within 18 months of closing, with an expected $200 \par       million in annual synergies and gross margins consistent with onsemi's \par       long-term financial model. onsemi remains committed to maintaining its \par       existing capital return policy during the pendency period. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transaction Details\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the terms of the agreement, which has been unanimously approved by the Boards of Directors of both companies, Synaptics stockholders will receive 1.350 shares of onsemi common stock for each share of Synaptics common stock held at the time of closing, implying pro forma ownership of approximately 12% for Synaptics stockholders on a fully diluted basis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As part of the transaction, one member of the Synaptics Board of Directors is expected to join onsemi's Board of Directors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The transaction is expected to close in mid-2027, subject to approval by Synaptics stockholders, the receipt of required regulatory approvals and other customary conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 onsemi and Synaptics Reiterate Previously Provided Financial Outlooks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As part of today's announcement, onsemi is reiterating its financial outlook for the second fiscal quarter of 2026 provided on May 4, 2026. Synaptics is reiterating its financial outlook for the fiscal fourth quarter of 2026 provided on May 7, 2026.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Conference Call and Webcast Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 onsemi will host a conference call for the financial community at 5:00 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time (EDT) on June 25, 2026, to discuss the transaction announcement. A live webcast and related presentation materials will be available on onsemi's IR site at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onsemi.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.onsemi.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . The webcast replay and presentation will be available following the call. Investors and interested parties can also access the conference call by pre-registering here \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=KFx-Ndgkpnx4G9NYQp6IMPRoToWTHPbXGI_rXhe3uSuyxJY5H1phGnxfCkiycD0lMRL8FyoypLthXTy3ELnwSzWKuZJ_LNQBam2A1kq_2HDDxqoJoFAgukC6kRcsbjc2wKDV9CU62-WG9yHEuxPq6Z_kXekrhKgOx2sB8RNu2bo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=KFx-Ndgkpnx4G9NYQp6IMPRoToWTHPbXGI_rXhe3uSuyxJY5H1phGnxfCkiycD0lMRL8FyoypLthXTy3ELnwSzWKuZJ_LNQBam2A1kq_2HDDxqoJoFAgukC6kRcsbjc2wKDV9CU62-WG9yHEuxPq6Z_kXekrhKgOx2sB8RNu2bo}}}\uc2 \f2 = .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Advisors\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley served as lead financial advisor to onsemi. J.P. Morgan Securities LLC also served as a financial advisor and Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP served as legal counsel to onsemi. Qatalyst Partners acted as exclusive financial advisor and Baker McKenzie served as legal counsel to Synaptics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 About onsemi\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 onsemi (Nasdaq: ON) delivers intelligent power and sensing technologies that enable electrification, energy efficiency, safety, and automation across automotive, industrial, and AI data center end-markets. With a highly differentiated and innovative product portfolio, onsemi helps customers solve complex challenges to achieve higher efficiency, improved performance, and lower system cost, while supporting a safer, cleaner, and more energy--efficient world. The company is part of the S&P 500(R) index. Learn more at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onsemi.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.onsemi.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 About Synaptics Incorporated\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Synaptics (Nasdaq: SYNA) is driving innovation in AI at the Edge, bringing AI closer to end users and transforming how we engage with intelligent connected devices, whether at home, at work, or on the move. As a go-to partner for forward-thinking product innovators, Synaptics powers the future with its cutting-edge Synaptics Astra(TM) AI-Native embedded compute, wireless connectivity, and multimodal sensing solutions. We're making the digital experience smarter, faster, more intuitive, secure, and seamless. From touch, display, and biometrics to AI-driven wireless connectivity, video, vision, audio, speech, and security processing, Synaptics is a force behind the next generation of technology enhancing how we live, work, and play.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Contact Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parag Agarwal\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vice President - Investor Relations & Corporate Development\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 onsemi\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (602) 244-3437\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investor@onsemi.com \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=tQgPe3-SDfw8xuXoFjPZMX0F_oJUc4jVbby6Vx28BJZCoBcBVtdogVB5tF0TD75gypF8xnUZxMif_QRAq17D5r9tHsWWqjxaIUB2